5363 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 5364 0 R/Alt(Focused Brake poster portion. The title states that Brake makes an antiviral protein from an RNA template and asks how a region without a conventional effector gene restricts phage propagation. A large logarithmic plot shows matched infectious phage yields for empty vector, intact Brake and inactive reverse transcriptase. Below it, two lines state that disrupting translation leaves the DNA but loses defence and that supplying the protein separately restores defence. The conclusion says that the protein mediates growth arrest and phage restriction and that its molecular target remains unknown.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[1]/Pg 12685 0 R>>
endobj
